\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord Christ, when first Thou cam'st to men,
\par Upon a Cross they bound Thee;
\par And mocked Thy saving Kingship then
\par By thorns with which they crowned Thee:
\par And still our wrongs may weave Thee now
\par New thorns to pierce that steady brow,
\par And robe of sorrow round Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O awful love which found no room
\par In life where sin denied Thee,
\par And, doomed to death, must bring to doom
\par The power which crucified Thee,
\par Till not a stone was left on stone,
\par And all a nation's pride o'erthrown,
\par Went down to dust beside Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. New advent of the love of Christ,
\par Shall we again refuse Thee,
\par Till in the night of hate and war
\par We perish as we lose Thee?
\par From old unfaith our souls release
\par To seek the Kingdom of Thy peace,
\par By which alone we choose Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O wounded hands of Jesus, build
\par In us Thy new creation;
\par Our pride is dust, our vaunt is stilled,
\par We wait Thy revelation:
\par O love that triumphs over loss,
\par We bring our hearts before Thy Cross,
\par To finish Thy salvation.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

